            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Pin skill versions and review updates</h2>
<p>Skills installed from GitHub now remember the exact commit they came from. Check for updates when you choose, see what changes before installing, pin a version, or roll back to an earlier one. Every step goes through Review → Apply.</p>
<h2>Updates open in What's New</h2>
<p>When an update is available, FullHouse shows its release notes in the What's New window, with download progress and buttons to cancel or install. Installation waits while changes are queued or Apply is running. Update notices in the library now match its width and theme.</p>
<h3>New</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Codex picks up MCP runtime updates (Labs)</strong> — An opt-in Labs setting lets FullHouse reload its own MCP servers in a running Codex after Apply, so runtime updates take effect without restarting Codex.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Improved</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Catch setup problems earlier</strong> — Settings now warns when a terminal Codex or OpenCode CLI lags far behind its desktop app, when links still point into the previous managed config folder, when Codex sees two skills with the same name, and when the MCP config in your home folder still uses the older Store setup. Configuration warnings appear in Settings again.</li>
<li><strong>Import a single SKILL.md</strong> — Add Skill → From Disk accepts a single SKILL.md or Markdown file as well as a folder, by drag and drop or the file picker.</li>
<li><strong>Confirm large worktree setups</strong> — When many existing worktrees would get tool connections at once, FullHouse first shows a summary to confirm. Not now keeps them on hold across launches; conflicts stay in Review.</li>
<li><strong>OpenRouter keys are reused</strong> — Adding an OpenRouter model reuses a key you have already saved, and Settings → Tokens shows the OpenRouter key status.</li>
<li><strong>Plugins section removed</strong> — The Plugins section is gone. Skills and MCP servers from enabled Codex plugins still appear in Skills and MCP, and existing plugin files stay where they are.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>GPT-5 and o-series via Eliza work in OpenCode</strong> — The Eliza OpenAI provider for OpenCode now uses the OpenAI package, so GPT-5, o-series and Responses-only models no longer fail with reasoningSummary or max_tokens errors. Update the Eliza OpenAI provider in the library to apply it.</li>
</ul>
